05:22.860 --> 05:24.560
...are a bit lacking.

05:22.860 --> 05:24.560
-Super hot me, set me afire

05:24.560 --> 05:26.490
-Frankly, I think it's holding them back.

05:24.560 --> 05:26.490
-Super hot me, set me afire

05:26.490 --> 05:30.030
-Huh, what did you say?

05:26.490 --> 05:30.030
-Out of this world, this perfect stage

05:30.030 --> 05:31.630
Spice up my flight

05:31.630 --> 05:33.100
I'm not holding back, check it out

05:33.100 --> 05:36.200
Ryusuke-kun's guys
are getting pretty good.

05:36.200 --> 05:41.940
You think? Bands like this
are a dime a dozen in Japan.

05:41.940 --> 05:45.610
Looks like a tough sell to
promote a band out of this joint.

05:47.020 --> 05:49.520
Squeeze your sweat yeah

05:49.520 --> 05:51.610
Blow your mind

05:57.560 --> 06:01.460
What, I fronted the studio fees last time.

06:03.270 --> 06:05.200
The nerve of you!

06:05.200 --> 06:08.170
You owe me 60,000 yen!

06:08.170 --> 06:11.940
By the way, what are we going to do
about our van's safety check?

06:11.940 --> 06:14.380
I'm broke already this month.

06:14.380 --> 06:15.910
I'm broke too!

06:15.910 --> 06:20.970
Hey, hey, we can't break up
just 'cause we're broke.

06:22.880 --> 06:27.180
Looks like we need more customers
to keep things going.

06:28.920 --> 06:31.530
That may be the toughest thing to do.

06:31.530 --> 06:33.830
-Taira-kun...
-Huh?

06:33.830 --> 06:37.070
Where can we find
some money lying around?

06:37.070 --> 06:38.760
I'm outta here.

06:42.470 --> 06:46.980
Oh, Togo-kun. I'm counting on you
to design our next flyer!

06:46.980 --> 06:51.110
Yeah. Well, I've got to go drop her off.

06:55.650 --> 07:00.380
Seems Beck is trapped in a
Mobius strip of the unpopular bands.

07:01.390 --> 07:04.520
Mobius strip? What do you mean?

07:10.430 --> 07:12.430
This is bad!

07:12.430 --> 07:14.470
What's the matter?

07:14.470 --> 07:16.710
Hey, don't scare us.

07:16.710 --> 07:20.440
T-t-that Tanaka creep...

07:29.020 --> 07:33.290
Hey, you! What a crappy start!

07:33.290 --> 07:36.730
Need to raise the pitch, you idiot!

07:36.730 --> 07:41.060
Your left hand's not
grabbing the water, fool!

07:41.060 --> 07:44.620
Your timing is way off!

07:51.370 --> 07:53.170
-Go for it!
-Go!

08:03.420 --> 08:07.690
Moron! Don't take a breath
right after the turn!

08:07.690 --> 08:11.190
Hey! Your kicking is getting weak!

08:11.190 --> 08:14.290
Kick like your life depends on it!

08:22.700 --> 08:25.470
-All right!
-He did it!

08:25.470 --> 08:28.210
Hey, isn't Tanaka-kun incredible?!

08:28.210 --> 08:31.150
He's seriously awesome!

08:31.150 --> 08:37.890
The results are in. In first place
is grade 9-D, Kohei Takahashi.

08:37.890 --> 08:43.190
Second place, Grade 9-A, Yukio Tanaka.

08:43.190 --> 08:47.630
Third place, Grade 9-B, Kazuo Watanabe.

08:50.200 --> 08:54.540
We'll shame him in the 100m backstroke.

08:54.540 --> 08:57.640
We'll show him what the
swim school training is made of!

08:57.640 --> 09:00.610
We're going to crush Tanaka!

09:00.610 --> 09:05.580
What was that touch earlier?!
You had one stroke too many!

09:05.580 --> 09:07.780
Saito-san, where're we going?

09:07.780 --> 09:13.050
Practice your start in the 25m pool!
Until time's up!

09:13.050 --> 09:19.160
I'm sorry...I'm...cramping...already...

09:19.160 --> 09:23.570
Hey...Hey! Koyuki!
Koyuki! Ko-Koyuki-kun?

09:23.570 --> 09:25.900
You're incredible, Koyuki!

09:28.000 --> 09:31.340
I was cheering for you
the whole time from the stands.

09:34.710 --> 09:37.280
I'll help you stretch.

09:37.280 --> 09:39.970
Koyuki, lie on your stomach.

09:41.020 --> 09:42.550
Okay...

09:42.550 --> 09:44.780
Koyuki, you were great!

09:47.020 --> 09:52.790
By the way, I heard that
Togo-kun might quit the band.

09:52.790 --> 09:55.560
Huh? But, why?

09:55.560 --> 09:59.700
He's getting a lot of pressure
from his parents and his girlfriend.

09:59.700 --> 10:02.340
Seems they want him to help out
with the family business.

10:02.340 --> 10:04.340
Yeah?

10:04.340 --> 10:08.180
That's why he hasn't been
coming to practice lately.

10:08.180 --> 10:09.940
Okay, face forward.

10:12.050 --> 10:14.620
Then what's going
to happen with the drums?

10:14.620 --> 10:16.650
Don't know.

10:16.650 --> 10:21.060
This might be the end of Beck.

10:21.060 --> 10:26.580
It's tough, you know, turning professional.

10:29.600 --> 10:31.900
All right, stretching completed!

10:34.970 --> 10:36.300
Thanks!

10:38.140 --> 10:42.010
I'll swim my best!

10:42.010 --> 10:47.520
My stretching isn't free!
That'll be 10,500 yen, tax inclusive!

10:47.520 --> 10:49.140
What?!

10:50.390 --> 10:54.620
Hey, let's do that, if Koyuki loses!

10:54.620 --> 11:01.900
But, if he does win, I'd like
to see Maho-chan give him a reward.

11:01.900 --> 11:06.630
Let's make a wager!
It'll raise his motivation level!

11:06.630 --> 11:07.970
But...

11:07.970 --> 11:09.370
Okay!

11:10.640 --> 11:15.110
If Koyuki wins this tournament,
I'll do whatever he asks.

11:15.110 --> 11:17.700
Eh?! Maho...

11:31.190 --> 11:35.360
On your mark, get set...

11:50.680 --> 11:53.080
Swim like your life depends on it!

11:57.890 --> 11:58.990
Koyuki!

11:58.990 --> 12:01.260
Tanaka-kun! Go for it!

12:01.260 --> 12:03.760
Tanaka! Come on!

12:03.760 --> 12:05.280
Wow...

12:12.930 --> 12:15.370
Koyuki! You'll be disgraced
if you lose!

12:15.370 --> 12:17.570
Go get 'em!

12:36.460 --> 12:38.460
Tanaka-kun!

12:38.460 --> 12:40.620
-Go for it!
-Tanaka-kun!

12:42.100 --> 12:44.930
Hey, what're you going
to do about Tanaka?

12:44.930 --> 12:48.130
Damn, that Tanaka!

12:52.510 --> 12:54.070
Koyuki!

13:29.880 --> 13:35.040
First place is Grade 9-A, Yukio Tanaka!

13:41.690 --> 13:43.710
His time's not bad.

13:45.790 --> 13:47.420
Damn.

13:52.870 --> 13:55.530
Hey, what're we going to do?
This doesn't look good.

13:58.310 --> 14:00.400
Hey, Hyodo!

14:04.210 --> 14:06.110
"Health Room"

14:06.110 --> 14:08.080
"Health Room"

14:06.110 --> 14:08.080
Thank you very much.

14:08.080 --> 14:08.670
"Health Room"

14:09.050 --> 14:12.990
Well, when you get home,
put an ice pack on it.

14:12.990 --> 14:14.450
Right.

14:18.560 --> 14:20.760
Koyuki!

14:20.760 --> 14:21.860
That was incredible!

14:21.860 --> 14:25.030
Our class won the tournament
because you came in first place!

14:25.030 --> 14:27.600
I made...first place?

14:27.600 --> 14:29.700
Koyuki, you made first place!

14:31.470 --> 14:34.530
I...I've got to thank Saito-san.

14:35.540 --> 14:38.570
-He's still at the pool.
-Yeah.

14:44.820 --> 14:47.160
Isn't that...Momoko-sensei?

14:47.160 --> 14:48.590
That's right.

14:48.590 --> 14:51.720
Seems she asked him to teach her.

14:54.860 --> 14:58.420
I hope things go well between those two.

15:16.350 --> 15:19.620
-It seems interesting.
-Yeah, I guess.

15:19.620 --> 15:21.780
Oh, Togo-san!

15:31.130 --> 15:33.660
Take care, Koyuki.

15:40.010 --> 15:42.010
Togo-san...

15:42.010 --> 15:44.910
Yeah...can't be helped.

15:44.910 --> 15:48.680
He's quitting the band to help out
with his family's business.

15:48.680 --> 15:51.220
Ryusuke-kun...

15:51.220 --> 15:54.620
Well, it's a tough world.

15:54.620 --> 15:59.920
To think someone good like
Togo-san would be quitting...

16:03.530 --> 16:05.430
Isn't it time for your rehearsal-

16:05.430 --> 16:09.030
Stupid! How can we rehearse
without a drummer?

16:19.410 --> 16:23.890
I guess I could spend the day
re-reading "Happy Sangokushi."

16:23.890 --> 16:28.650
Let's see...How far did I get again?

16:54.750 --> 16:58.290
Powerful and straightforward...
And with feeling.

16:58.290 --> 17:00.890
Saku's on the drums?!

17:00.890 --> 17:02.450
Saku...

17:29.980 --> 17:32.820
How long have you been
playing the drums?

17:32.820 --> 17:36.020
Since I was seven, after my older brother.

17:36.020 --> 17:39.260
Oh yeah? Are you from a musical family?

17:39.260 --> 17:44.170
No, not at all.
My brother's into baseball now.

17:44.170 --> 17:45.170
I see.

17:45.170 --> 17:49.100
I'm completely self-taught,
so I'm not very confident.

17:52.140 --> 17:53.970
Saku...

17:56.440 --> 17:57.910
Yo!

17:57.910 --> 17:59.450
You're late, Chiba!

17:59.450 --> 18:05.420
Yeah, I wanted Togo-kun to reconsider.
So I went to talk to him.

18:05.420 --> 18:07.490
And?

18:07.490 --> 18:08.850
Not gonna happen.

18:10.420 --> 18:12.520
Well, can't be helped.

18:14.560 --> 18:17.830
Why are you sitting there?

18:20.970 --> 18:23.400
What?! Those two?!

18:23.400 --> 18:27.540
Yeah, I want to make Koyuki and Saku
part of our support members.

18:27.540 --> 18:31.350
But they're only in intermediate school.

18:31.350 --> 18:34.780
Saku might be okay,
but Koyuki's nowhere near our level.

18:36.220 --> 18:40.990
After hearing Saku's drums today,
I wanted to take a gamble on them.

18:40.990 --> 18:47.800
Gamble? With Togo gone,
this whole band could go under.

18:47.800 --> 18:51.730
Technical skill alone
doesn't make a band.

18:53.030 --> 18:56.030
What's important...is the "chemistry."

19:00.010 --> 19:03.410
Ryusuke-kun mentioned "chemistry."

19:03.410 --> 19:07.210
"Chemistry"-like a chemical reaction?

19:07.210 --> 19:09.610
I can just see a huge explosion!

19:10.750 --> 19:12.450
Ka-boom!

19:17.560 --> 19:19.430
You guys haven't heard?

19:19.430 --> 19:23.260
We're performing live a week from now?

19:23.260 --> 19:24.730
But we haven't practiced long...

19:24.730 --> 19:27.570
It's an event with some
serious attendance.

19:27.570 --> 19:33.570
We're gonna wow the crowd and
take the other bands' customers!

19:33.570 --> 19:35.140
-Oh...
-Oh...

19:35.140 --> 19:38.850
So we're gonna practice extra hard,
starting tomorrow.

19:38.850 --> 19:42.080
Hey, Chiba-kun! Pay up, won't you?

19:42.080 --> 19:45.080
Huh? Don't got none.

20:01.500 --> 20:02.990
Check it out!

20:04.340 --> 20:05.500
Yeah!

20:06.440 --> 20:09.270
Hey! You're off beat!

20:41.010 --> 20:43.910
What, you want me to carry this?!

20:43.910 --> 20:46.280
Ouch...

20:47.380 --> 20:49.350
Hey, are you all right?

20:49.350 --> 20:52.250
I think I'm just a bit nervous.

20:52.250 --> 20:55.320
Hey, are you getting nervous
about carrying in the equipment?

20:55.320 --> 20:59.560
Come on, everyone gets nervous
before playing a gig.

20:59.560 --> 21:05.570
Even Jimi Hendrix, Jimmy Page,
Flea, Tom Morello...

21:05.570 --> 21:08.040
Everyone's the same.

21:08.040 --> 21:13.440
But, I heard that the Stones
play billiards before playing live...

21:13.440 --> 21:15.870
They do that to ease the tension.

21:18.180 --> 21:21.020
Saku...Wanna go shoot some pool?

21:21.020 --> 21:23.580
Huh? What about the rehearsal?

21:40.730 --> 21:46.370
The bands that were rehearsing
before us were all really good.

21:47.470 --> 21:50.410
Okay, Beck! It's your turn.

21:53.950 --> 21:56.880
During rehearsal,
we check the sound balance.

21:56.880 --> 22:01.380
First we do the drums,
and my vocals get done last.

22:08.230 --> 22:12.260
Oh well, I've got to do my very best now.

22:26.780 --> 22:30.650
The guitar, please. 15 minutes left.

22:50.340 --> 22:52.440
Another minute

22:52.440 --> 22:55.140
Feelin' so fine

22:57.450 --> 22:59.680
You turn the freeze

22:59.680 --> 23:02.410
into warm light

23:04.520 --> 23:08.090
Had a premonition

23:08.090 --> 23:10.790
I've been waitin' ever since

23:10.790 --> 23:14.300
My world comin' down

23:14.300 --> 23:17.100
It's got me spinnin' 'round

23:18.870 --> 23:25.040
If you really wanna fly

23:25.040 --> 23:27.810
you gotta let go

23:40.060 --> 23:42.390
Simply the most

23:42.390 --> 23:44.430
big sensation

23:44.430 --> 23:47.230
(once you're here you won't go back)

23:47.230 --> 23:49.500
She's really pretty

23:49.500 --> 23:51.500
One-eyed vision

23:51.500 --> 23:54.340
(lose the fear it don't come back)

23:54.340 --> 23:57.840
Little sister showed me

23:57.840 --> 24:00.510
Really took me for a ride

24:00.510 --> 24:02.180
My world comin' down

24:02.180 --> 24:05.520
(once you're here you won't go back)

24:05.520 --> 24:09.540
(lose the fear it don't come back)

24:13.860 --> 24:16.260
-This is Okute-san of Le Mans Porche!
-We're this week's musicians!

24:16.260 --> 24:17.430
"Next Episode"

24:16.260 --> 24:17.430
-This is Okute-san of Le Mans Porche!
-We're this week's musicians!

24:17.430 --> 24:20.190
"Next Episode"

24:17.430 --> 24:20.190
Go, Le Mans Porche! Nice to meet you!
